---
// The long garage on the home page (Dan 2026-11-18: live on Nov 19 to half the laptop visitors, an A/B test of
// whether it sells). The room is the unlisted /garage-9f3c/ page (tools/_home-opening/room.html, copied by
// tools/garagepage) in embed mode, in a fixed frame behind the page; this page's own scroll walks it down the aisle.
// The frame gets the room as srcdoc, not as a URL: the site sends X-Frame-Options: DENY and a CSP frame-src without
// 'self' (Cloudflare), which refuse any framed page of ours; a srcdoc document is not fetched, so neither applies.
// It inherits this page's origin and CSP (the same policy the room already runs under on its own URL).
// At the end of the walk the room's TV face covers the screen under the nav, exactly where the real TV (WordWall)
// sits, and the real TV fades in over it; past that point the frame is hidden and paused.
// The picture on the room's TV is this page's own TV, photographed here in the visitor's browser while the room loads
// (the script's "the room's picture of the TV", 2026-11-21), so the two are the same picture at any window size; the
// room's saved photos of the TV (tools/_home-opening/tvcap.mjs, three screen sizes) show until it is taken, or if it fails.
//
// Who sees it: laptops and desktops (1000 px wide, a mouse or trackpad, WebGL 2), no reduced motion, no data saver,
// no bot. Half of them, drawn once and kept (localStorage ra-home); phones keep today's home page (Dan 2026-11-08).
// Once a session: a visitor who walked to the TV (or skipped) gets the TV straight away on the next home visit.
// ra-home-seen = the side this visitor was drawn into ('garage' | 'tv'), whatever happened next; ra-home-outcome = how
// the garage went ('started' | 'walked' to the TV | 'skipped' | 'fallback'). The cart sends both to Paddle
// (customData.home, customData.home_out), so the test reads both ways: by the draw, and by what was really seen.
// ?home=garage / ?home=tv pins a variant on this browser (testing; its own key, ra-home-pin: a pin never touches the
// draw or the two keys above, and the cart sends nothing for a pinned browser); ?home=off forgets it all.
// SHARE = the garage's share of the visitors drawn. 0 = off for everyone but a ?home=garage pin, visitors already drawn
// 'garage' included (a soft launch, or the switch if the room misbehaves live); nobody is drawn while it is 0.
// Taking it off the site altogether = revert the HomeOpening import and tag in src/pages/index.astro.
// Safety: the room says 'ready' (or 'error') by postMessage; no 'ready' in 45 s of the tab being looked at, an error
// first, or the Skip button (after 6 s of loading) puts the normal home page back.
---

<div class="ho" id="ho">
  <iframe class="ho-frame" id="hoFrame" title="The RevAudio garage" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"></iframe>
  <button class="ho-skip" id="hoSkip" type="button">Skip to the plugins <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></button>
</div>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var SHARE = 0; // soft launch (Dan 2026-11-18, "two stages"): only a ?home=garage pin, until the room runs smoothly and he looks again
    var H = document.documentElement, KEY = 'ra-home', SEEN = 'ra-home-seen', PIN = 'ra-home-pin', DONE = 'ra-ho-done';
    var ls = function (k, v) { try { if (v === undefined) return localStorage.getItem(k); if (v === null) localStorage.removeItem(k); else localStorage.setItem(k, v); } catch (e) {} return null; };
    var ss = function (k, v) { try { if (v === undefined) return sessionStorage.getItem(k); sessionStorage.setItem(k, v); } catch (e) {} return null; };
    var q = null; try { q = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('home'); } catch (e) {}
    if (q === 'garage' || q === 'tv') ls(PIN, q);
    if (q === 'off') { ls(PIN, null); ls(KEY, null); ls(SEEN, null); ls('ra-home-outcome', null); }
    var pin = q === 'garage' || q === 'tv' ? q : ls(PIN); // (a pin works even where site data is blocked)
    if (pin !== 'garage' && pin !== 'tv') pin = null;
    var forced = q === 'garage';
    if (!pin && !(SHARE > 0)) return; // SHARE 0: pins only, whatever was drawn before
    var v = pin || ls(KEY);
    var ok = false;
    try {
      ok = matchMedia('(min-width: 1000px) and (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)').matches
        && !matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches
        && !H.classList.contains('hc') // (high contrast, set in BaseLayout's head: as the site's other scenes)
        && !(navigator.connection && navigator.connection.saveData)
        && !navigator.webdriver
        && !/bot|crawl|spider|slurp|lighthouse|headless|preview|facebookexternalhit/i.test(navigator.userAgent);
      // the WebGL 2 check costs 10 to 40 ms: only where the room could open now (not for 'tv', not once it was walked)
      if (ok && !forced && v !== 'tv' && !(v === 'garage' && ss(DONE))) {
        var gl = document.createElement('canvas').getContext('webgl2');
        ok = !!gl;
        var lose = gl && gl.getExtension('WEBGL_lose_context'); if (lose) lose.loseContext();
      }
    } catch (e) { ok = false; }
    if (!ok && !forced) return; // phones, bots, no WebGL 2: today's home page, not in the test
    if (!pin) {
      if (v !== 'garage' && v !== 'tv') { v = Math.random() < SHARE ? 'garage' : 'tv'; ls(KEY, v); }
      ls(SEEN, v);
    }
    if (v !== 'garage') return;
    if (ss(DONE) && !forced) return; // walked it once this session: the TV straight away
    H.classList.add('ho-on', 'ho-loading');
    history.scrollRestoration = 'manual';
  })();
</script>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var H = document.documentElement;
    if (!H.classList.contains('ho-on')) return;
    var ho = document.getElementById('ho'), frame = document.getElementById('hoFrame'), skip = document.getElementById('hoSkip');
    var wall = null, ready = false, booted = false, state = '', paused = false, pauseTimer = 0, raf = 0;
    var walkPx = innerHeight * 3.7, lockY = 0, lastY = 0, down = false, landTimer = 0, waited = 0, focusAt = -1e4, leftAt = 0, leftY = 0;
    var px = function (name) { return parseFloat(getComputedStyle(H).getPropertyValue(name)) || 0; };
    var navTotal = function () { return Math.round((px('--site-nav-h') || 41) + px('--sale-h')); };
    function done() { try { sessionStorage.setItem('ra-ho-done', '1'); } catch (e) {} }
    // how the garage went for this visitor, for the test's readout (the cart sends it); never for a tester's pin
    function note(o) { try { if (!localStorage.getItem('ra-home-pin')) localStorage.setItem('ra-home-outcome', o); } catch (e) {} }
    // the site's scroller (Lenis; the module script below hands it over once it has loaded) and a jump it can't undo
    function lenis() { return window.__hoLenis ? window.__hoLenis() : null; }
    function jump(y) {
      var l = lenis(); if (l) l.scrollTo(y, { immediate: true, force: true });
      if (Math.abs(scrollY - y) > 1) scrollTo(0, y);
    }
    function room() { try { return frame.contentWindow && frame.contentWindow.__garage; } catch (e) { return null; } }
    function pause(b) { if (paused === b) return; paused = b; var r = room(); if (r) r.pause(b); }
    function setState(s) {
      if (s === state) return;
      var was = state;
      state = s;
      H.classList.toggle('ho-locked', s === 'locked');
      clearTimeout(pauseTimer);
      if (s === 'walk') {
        H.classList.remove('ho-past'); pause(false);
        if (wall && wall.contains(document.activeElement)) document.activeElement.blur(); // (focus doesn't stay in the TV, unseen again)
        if (was === 'locked') { leftAt = performance.now(); leftY = scrollY; hold(); }
        return;
      }
      wall.style.translate = '';
      done(); note('walked');
      requestAnimationFrame(follow);
      // the real TV has faded in over the room's: the room hides and stops drawing
      pauseTimer = setTimeout(function () { H.classList.add('ho-past'); pause(true); }, 600);
    }
    function measure() {
      ho.style.setProperty('--ho-walk', walkPx + 'px');
      wall = wall || document.querySelector('.garage-wall');
      if (wall) { wall.style.translate = ''; lockY = wall.getBoundingClientRect().top + scrollY - navTotal(); } // (its place in the page, without hold()'s shift)
      window.__hoLockY = lockY; // (the welcome popup measures its 35 % from here: the home page below the walk)
    }
    function onScroll() {
      raf = 0;
      var y = scrollY, p = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, 1 - (lockY - y) / walkPx));
      // (the browser brings a control it just focused into view by itself, Safari to the middle of the screen: for one
      // in the TV that can be short of the lock)
      if (p < 0.999 && performance.now() - focusAt < 400 && toTv()) return;
      if (!ready) return;
      var r = room(); if (r) r.to(p);
      setState(p >= 0.999 ? 'locked' : 'walk');
      place();
    }
    // past the lock the room goes up with the page, so its TV stays under the real one while that fades in (a wheel
    // carries on through the lock: a still room showed two TVs apart); and it shows only behind the TV, never over the
    // sections under it
    function place() {
      var y = scrollY, past = state === 'locked' ? Math.max(0, y - lockY) : 0;
      var cut = state === 'locked' ? Math.max(0, Math.round(innerHeight - (lockY - y + past + navTotal() + wall.offsetHeight))) : 0;
      frame.style.transform = past ? 'translateY(' + -past + 'px)' : '';
      frame.style.clipPath = cut ? 'inset(0 0 ' + cut + 'px 0)' : '';
    }
    // (every frame while the two cross-fade: Safari's scroll event comes a frame or two after the page moved)
    function follow() { if (state === 'locked' && !H.classList.contains('ho-past')) { place(); requestAnimationFrame(follow); } }
    // back up into the walk, its mirror: for the 0.2 s the real TV takes to fade out it stays where it was on the screen,
    // over the room's TV, while the page goes on down under the wheel (the room's TV does move as the walk backs off:
    // a pixel or two on a slow scroll, about 15 px by the end of the fade on a hard wheel)
    function hold() {
      var on = state === 'walk' && performance.now() - leftAt < 220;
      wall.style.translate = on ? '0 ' + (scrollY - leftY).toFixed(1) + 'px' : '';
      if (on) requestAnimationFrame(hold);
    }
    // the end of the walk is the room's picture of the TV, which does nothing: a walk that stops in its last tenth
    // glides on to the lock (the TV's own landing, WordWall.astro, leaves the walk to this one; like it, never against
    // the visitor: only when the last move was down)
    function land() {
      var l = lenis();
      if (l && l.isScrolling === 'smooth') { landTimer = setTimeout(land, 160); return; } // still gliding: ask again
      if (!ready || state !== 'walk' || !down || lockY - scrollY > 0.1 * walkPx || document.querySelector('dialog[open]')) return;
      var y = Math.ceil(lockY);
      if (l) l.scrollTo(y, { duration: 0.55, easing: function (t) { return 1 - Math.pow(1 - t, 4); } }); else scrollTo(0, y);
    }
    function fallback(skipped) { // today's home page, now
      if (!H.classList.contains('ho-on')) return;
      done(); note(skipped === true ? 'skipped' : 'fallback');
      H.classList.remove('ho-on', 'ho-loading', 'ho-locked', 'ho-past');
      clearTimeout(slow); clearInterval(give); clearTimeout(landTimer);
      removeEventListener('scroll', queue);
      try { frame.src = 'about:blank'; } catch (e) {}
      ho.remove();
      scrollTo(0, 0);
      history.scrollRestoration = 'auto'; // (today's page from here on: Back to it finds its place again)
      // the Skip button went with the room: the focus it held goes to the TV it promised
      var tag = skipped === true && document.querySelector('.garage-wall .ww-tag'); if (tag) tag.focus({ preventScroll: true });
    }
    function queue() {
      if (!raf) raf = requestAnimationFrame(onScroll);
      var y = scrollY; if (y !== lastY) { down = y > lastY; lastY = y; }
      clearTimeout(landTimer); landTimer = setTimeout(land, 160);
    }
    // keyboard and screen readers reach the TV as on today's page (it is there, unseen, all along): focus inside it
    // lands the page on the lock, where it shows. Not over a glide (the nav's Plugins link is on its way there)
    function toTv() {
      var l = lenis();
      if ((l && l.isScrolling === 'smooth') || !H.classList.contains('ho-on') || !wall || !wall.contains(document.activeElement) || lockY - scrollY <= 0.001 * walkPx) return false;
      jump(Math.ceil(lockY)); return true;
    }
    document.addEventListener('focusin', function (e) { if (wall && wall.contains(e.target)) { focusAt = performance.now(); toTv(); } });
    addEventListener('message', function (e) {
      if (e.origin !== location.origin || e.source !== frame.contentWindow || !e.data || !e.data.garage) return;
      var m = e.data;
      if (m.walkPx) {
        // a resize mid-walk (the walk's length follows the screen's height) keeps the visitor's place in it
        var left = ready && state === 'walk' && m.walkPx !== walkPx ? (lockY - scrollY) / walkPx : -1;
        walkPx = m.walkPx; measure();
        if (left >= 0) jump(Math.max(0, Math.round(lockY - left * walkPx)));
      }
      if (m.garage === 'boot') booted = true;
      if (m.garage === 'error' && !ready) fallback();
      if (m.garage === 'ready' && !ready) {
        ready = true;
        clearTimeout(slow); clearInterval(give);
        skip.classList.remove('is-up');
        H.classList.remove('ho-loading');
        measure(); onScroll();
      }
    });
    addEventListener('scroll', queue, { passive: true });
    // the loading screen holds the page still: the wheel never reaches the site's Lenis while it shows
    addEventListener('wheel', function (e) { if (H.classList.contains('ho-loading')) { e.preventDefault(); e.stopImmediatePropagation(); } }, { capture: true, passive: false });
    // the room never started (a script failed to load), or its loading screen gave up on a stall: today's home page
    frame.addEventListener('load', function () {
      try { if (frame.contentWindow.location.href !== 'about:srcdoc') return; } catch (e) {} // (the frame's first, empty page)
      setTimeout(function () { if (!booted && !ready) fallback(); }, 1500);
    });
    var watch = setInterval(function () {
      if (ready || !H.classList.contains('ho-on')) { clearInterval(watch); return; }
      try { var d = frame.contentDocument; if (booted && d && !room() && !d.documentElement.classList.contains('lights-loading')) fallback(); /* (room() is set just before 'ready') */ } catch (e) {}
    }, 1000);
    addEventListener('resize', function () { measure(); queue(); });
    skip.addEventListener('click', function () { if (!ready) fallback(true); }); // (not in the 0.3 s it takes to fade out once the room is up)
    // Skip comes up after 6 s of loading, but not as the room is about to take over: once the loading screen's last light
    // bank is on (its log, lights/lights-on.js) the hand-off is a second or two away, and the button flashed up and out
    // (11-20). It waits 3 s more, once: a load that stalls after the last bank still gets its Skip
    function lastBank() { try { var w = frame.contentWindow; return w.lightsOn.log.length > w.LIGHT_BANKS.length; } catch (e) { return false; } }
    var slow = setTimeout(function up() {
      if (ready) return;
      if (!up.waited && lastBank()) { up.waited = true; slow = setTimeout(up, 3000); return; }
      skip.classList.add('is-up');
    }, 6000);
    // 45 s of the tab being looked at: one opened in the background loads when the visitor comes to it (its room
    // waits for frames a hidden tab doesn't draw)
    var give = setInterval(function () { if (!ready && !document.hidden && (waited += 1000) >= 45000) fallback(); }, 1000);
    scrollTo(0, 0);
    measure();
    note('started');
    // the room's picture of the TV: this page photographs its own TV while the room loads (tv-photo.js, with the why
    // and the how, and the library it uses; both beside the room's files, fetched together, run in this order, only
    // here). window.__hoTv says how it went (the checks read it). Either file missing: the room keeps its saved photo
    window.__hoTv = { state: 'waiting' };
    ['vendor/modern-screenshot/modern-screenshot-4.7.0.js', 'tv-photo.js'].forEach(function (f, i) {
      var s = document.createElement('script'); s.src = '/garage-9f3c/' + f; s.async = false;
      s.onerror = function () { window.__hoTv = { state: 'failed', why: 'no ' + f }; };
      if (i) s.onload = function () { try { window.__hoTvPhoto(frame, navTotal); } catch (e) { window.__hoTv = { state: 'failed', why: String(e && e.message || e) }; } };
      document.head.appendChild(s);
    });
    fetch('/garage-9f3c/', { credentials: 'same-origin' })
      .then(function (r) { if (!r.ok) throw new Error(r.status); return r.text(); })
      .then(function (html) {
        if (!H.classList.contains('ho-on')) return;
        // ?look=<id>: another look for the room than its own (room.html LOOK_DEFAULT, VHS since Dan's pick, 2026-11-18):
        // today (today's look, without one), vhs or vhs-more (the three being compared, 11-20; film and 16mm stay on
        // the room's own unlisted page); only an id on this list
        var look = null; try { look = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('look'); } catch (e) {}
        if (['today', 'vhs', 'vhs-more'].indexOf(look) < 0) look = '';
        // (and the room's embed class before its first paint: its own script adds it once its imports are in, and until
        // then its builder's Bench button showed on the black start of the loading screen)
        var head = '<base href="/garage-9f3c/"><script>window.__EMBED = { nav: ' + navTotal() + ', sale: \'' + (H.dataset.sale || (H.dataset.saleSoon ? 'soon' : '')).replace(/[^a-z]/g, '') + '\'' + (look ? ', look: \'' + look + '\'' : '') + ' }; document.documentElement.classList.add(\'embed\');<\/script>';
        frame.srcdoc = html
          .replace(/<head[^>]*>/i, function (m) { return m + head; })
          // the room's pictures of this page's nav, TV and below are not shown here; and the browser's early fetches in
          // a srcdoc ignore its <base> (Chrome asked /assets/..., /lights/... at the root), so the rest go absolute
          .replace(/ src="assets\/(nav|below|tv)-[^"]*"/g, '') // (the TV's saved photo for this screen's width comes from the room's resize(); this page's own photo of its TV takes its place, tv-photo.js)
          .replace(/ src="(assets|lights|vendor)\//g, ' src="/garage-9f3c/$1/');
      })
      .catch(fallback);
  })();
</script>

<script>
  // the site's scroller, for the inline script above (which has to run before any module loads)
  import { lenis } from '../lib/motion';
  (window as any).__hoLenis = () => lenis;
</script>

<style>
  .ho { display: none; }
  :global(html.ho-on) .ho { display: block; height: var(--ho-walk, 370vh); }
  .ho-frame { position: fixed; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100vh; border: 0; z-index: 1; pointer-events: none;
    background: #060509; color-scheme: dark; }
  :global(html.ho-past) .ho-frame { visibility: hidden; }
  /* the site's nav is glass (and the sale strip sits over it): over the room it let the room through, tinted by it,
     and went back to grey in the frame the room hid (11-20; sharp where the browser does not draw the blur). So a strip of the page's own dark lies between the room and the two, for as long as
     the room shows: the nav as over the top of any page. Back at once with the room; out slowly, the smoke that takes
     its place is a shade lighter */
  :global(html.ho-on) .ho::after { content: ''; position: fixed; inset: 0 0 auto; height: calc(var(--site-nav-h, 41px) + var(--sale-h, 0px));
    z-index: 1; background: var(--bg-0); pointer-events: none; }
  :global(html.ho-past) .ho::after { opacity: 0; visibility: hidden; transition: opacity .4s ease-out, visibility 0s .4s; }
  /* speed (2026-11-18, O-2): the site's smoke plates sit behind the opaque frame for the whole walk; unseen, they still
     cost the compositor about 3 ms a frame. They come back with ho-past, when the frame hides: over 0.4 s (11-20), not
     in one frame, which showed as the fog snapping on over the section under the TV */
  :global(html.ho-on:not(.ho-past) .haze) { visibility: hidden; opacity: 0; }
  :global(html.ho-on.ho-past .haze) { transition: opacity .4s ease-out; }
  /* the real TV waits, unseen, at the end of the walk; at the lock it fades in over the room's TV, and back up into the
     walk it fades out over it (0.2 s, 11-20: at once, the sharp TV became the room's softer one in one frame).
     Unseen, not hidden: it stays in the tab order and for screen readers (focus in it lands on the lock, the script
     above); until then nothing in it takes the mouse (its lit panel sets pointer-events and visibility of its own) */
  :global(html.ho-on .garage-wall) { position: relative; z-index: 2; opacity: 0; transition: opacity .2s ease-out; }
  :global(html.ho-on:not(.ho-locked) .garage-wall), :global(html.ho-on:not(.ho-locked) .garage-wall *) { pointer-events: none !important; }
  :global(html.ho-on.ho-locked .garage-wall) { opacity: 1; transition: opacity .45s ease-out; }
  :global(html.ho-loading), :global(html.ho-loading body) { overflow: hidden; scrollbar-gutter: stable; }
  .ho-skip { position: fixed; left: 50%; bottom: 28px; translate: -50% 0; z-index: 3; appearance: none; cursor: pointer;
    border: 1px solid rgba(232, 200, 120, 0.45); border-radius: 999px; background: rgba(12, 10, 8, 0.82); color: #e8dccb;
    font: 600 13px/1 Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.04em; padding: 12px 18px;
    opacity: 0; visibility: hidden; transition: opacity .3s ease, visibility 0s .3s; } /* (in and out over 0.3 s, 11-20: it popped) */
  .ho-skip.is-up { opacity: 1; visibility: visible; transition-delay: 0s; }
  .ho-skip:hover, .ho-skip:focus-visible { border-color: #e8c878; color: #fff3d6; }
</style>
